-- ============================================================
-- Physics: vocabulary seed and card mapping
--
-- APPROVED. 137 new CONTENT concepts, 4 new QUANTITATIVE objects, and a
-- PRIMARY mapping for all 444 physics flashcards. No REASONING object: the
-- approved design contains none.
--
-- WHY SO MANY. Physics is greenfield. Searching all 705 existing objects for
-- waves, optics, mechanics and circuits returns only biology and chemistry
-- concepts that share a word: "vascular resistance", "cell potential". Genuine
-- reuse is 10 objects over 27 cards, concentrated in thermodynamics and atomic
-- structure, which is where physics and chemistry really do teach one thing.
--
-- CATEGORIES. Five AAMC categories are created. FOUR are the physics 4-series
-- (4A-4D); 4E already existed and is reused, not duplicated. The fifth is 5E,
-- because physics thermodynamics is AAMC 5E and not part of the 4-series at
-- all. Names are the official AAMC wording, matching the full-sentence form
-- this ontology already uses for 4E, 5B and 5D.
--
-- QUANTITATIVE OBJECTS CARRY NO TAXONOMY. The four vector objects are
-- mathematical tools that happen to sit in a physics deck. Giving them a
-- physics discipline would be a fabrication, and the triggers from
-- 20260924_object_type.sql reject it outright.
--
-- PROVENANCE. Every card mapping is AI_PROPOSED. The vocabulary and the
-- clustering were approved; 444 individual rows were not reviewed one by one.
--
-- WRITE SCOPE. Concepts, their taxonomy, and flashcard_concepts. No learner
-- table is read or written.
-- ============================================================

BEGIN;

